clauses:
"RESOLVED, AS IT IS HEREBY RESOLVED, That the Corporation, through the majority members of the  Board of Directors authorize and direct, as it hereby authorizes and directs management to update its officers    on matters pertaining to official transactions with the DEPARTMENT OF MIGRANT WORKERS (DMW);

''RESOLVED FURTHER, That the Corporation has approved  the new designation of MR. ERNESTO B. MALLARI from  Fleet Manager (Tanker)/Operations Support Manager to Fleet Manager (Tanker) /Scholarship Officer and to be one of the authorized signatories of the company relevant to its documents being transacted in compliance with DEPARTMENT OF MIGRANT WORKERS (DMW);

"RESOLVED FINALLY, that the Corporate Secretary be directed, as he is hereby authorized and  directed to  furnish all  persons concerned copies of the foregoing resolution including but not limited to appropriate offices of the government and regulatory  agencies of the Philippines,  for its  reference, guidance  and for whatever lawful purpose it may serve.

“RESOLVED, AS IT IS HEREBY RESOLVED, That the corporation through the Board of Directors, authorize and direct, as it hereby authorizes and directs management to transact with the BUREAU OF INTERNAL REVENUE (“BIR”) - RDO 047 East Makati for purposes of its change of registered office address;
"RESOLVED FURTHER, That the corporation authorize and appoint, as it hereby authorizes and appoints its AVP for Finance, MS. ANGELICA R. TAN to sign for and on behalf of the corporation, all documents relative to the aforementioned corporate undertaking as well as MR. MARK ANTHONY D. REYES to be the authorized representative of the Corporation to transact, process and submit the necessary documents related to the aforesaid undertaking; 
“RESOLVED FINALLY, That the Corporate Secretary be directed, as he is hereby authorized and directed to furnish all persons concerned copies of the foregoing resolution.”

“RESOLVED, AS IT IS HEREBY RESOLVED, That the Corporation, through the Board of Directors, accept, as it hereby accepts with regrets the resignation of MR. TAKESHI MORIYAMA as Vice-President, effective April 30, 2026  and to extend to him a vote of gratitude for his  dedication and invaluable services rendered to the Corporation;
“RESOLVED FURTHER, That the Corporation through the Board of Directors appoints MR. HIROSHI NAKAGAWA     to replace MR. MORIYAMA  as  Vice -President effective  May 1, 2026. 

“RESOLVED FINALLY, that a Copy of this resolution will be furnished to appropriate offices of the government and regulatory agencies of the Philippines, for its reference, guidance and for whatever lawful purpose it may serve.”
